  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'If a^(2 − x) · b^(5x) = a^(x + 3) · b^(3x), show that x log(b/a) = (1/2) log a. (3 marks)', 'a^(2 − x) · b^(5x) = a^(x + 3) · b^(3x). Dividing, b^(5x − 3x) = a^(x + 3 − (2 − x)), i.e. b^(2x) = a^(2x + 1). Taking logarithms: 2x log b = (2x + 1) log a = 2x log a + log a. So 2x(log b − log a) = log a, i.e. 2x log(b/a) = log a, and x log(b/a) = (1/2) log a. Hence shown.', null, '[{"point": "Rearrange: b^(5x − 3x) = a^(x + 3 − 2 + x) → b^(2x) = a^(2x + 1)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Take logs: 2x log b = (2x + 1) log a", "marks": 1}, {"point": "2x(log b − log a) = log a → x log(b/a) = ½ log a", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
