  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'The coefficient of x in the equation x² + px + q = 0 was taken as 17 in place of 13, and its roots were found to be −2 and −15. Find the roots of the original equation. (3 marks)', 'Only the coefficient of x was taken wrongly, so the constant term is right: q = (−2)(−15) = 30. (Check: with p = 17 the sum of roots is −17 = −2 − 15 ✓.) The original equation is x² + 13x + 30 = 0, i.e. (x + 3)(x + 10) = 0, so its roots are −3 and −10.', null, '[{"point": "Constant term was correct: q = product of roots = (−2)(−15) = 30", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Original equation: x² + 13x + 30 = 0", "marks": 1}, {"point": "(x + 3)(x + 10) = 0 → roots −3 and −10", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
