  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'For the circuit diagram of a Wheatstone bridge shown in the figure (R₁ top-left, R₂ top-right, R₄ bottom-left, R₃ bottom-right, galvanometer G between the top and bottom junctions, cell across the left and right junctions), use Kirchhoff''s laws to obtain its balance condition. (3 marks)', 'Let the current from the cell divide at the left junction into I₁ (through R₁) and I₂ (through R₄). At balance the galvanometer shows no deflection, so Ig = 0; by Kirchhoff''s junction rule the current I₁ continues through R₂ and I₂ through R₃.
Applying Kirchhoff''s loop rule to the closed loop containing R₁, G and R₄ (with Ig = 0): I₁R₁ − I₂R₄ = 0, so I₁R₁ = I₂R₄ ... (1).
For the loop containing R₂, G and R₃: I₁R₂ − I₂R₃ = 0, so I₁R₂ = I₂R₃ ... (2).
Dividing (1) by (2): R₁/R₂ = R₄/R₃, i.e. R₁R₃ = R₂R₄. This is the balance condition of the Wheatstone bridge.', null, '[{"point": "At balance no current flows through G (Ig = 0): the current I₁ in R₁ also flows in R₂, and I₂ in R₄ also flows in R₃ (junction rule)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Loop rule: loop through R₁, G, R₄ → I₁R₁ = I₂R₄; loop through R₂, G, R₃ → I₁R₂ = I₂R₃", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Dividing: R₁/R₂ = R₄/R₃ (i.e. R₁R₃ = R₂R₄)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
